{
  "title": "Differential pair",
  "group": "Electronics — analog",
  "description": "differential pair: tanh transfer, sweep V(in+) with the tail current stepped 0.1/0.2/0.4 mA",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 60,
        "y": -173,
        "title": "Differential pair — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "A MOS differential pair: MN1 and MN2 share a tail",
          "current IT and load resistors RD1 = RD2 = 7.5 kohm to",
          "VDD = 5 V. VCM holds MN2's gate at 2.5 V while the",
          "sweep ramps VIN (MN1's gate) from 1.7 to 3.3 V.",
          "The pair steers IT between the two sides as a tanh of",
          "the input difference, so probes voutp and voutn split",
          "apart and cross at VIN = VCM. IT is stepped",
          "0.1/0.2/0.4 mA to show steeper transfer at more tail.",
          "",
          "Set VCM.V = 2.0 and re-run to move the crossover point."
        ]
      }
    ],
